# Cloudflare Pages Redirects & Internal Rewrites
# =================================================
# Generated for https://tipitakapali.org (static export)
# See export_static_cloudflare_pages.py:generate_cloudflare_redirects() and app/not-found.jsx

# 1. API Static Route Rewrites (Seamless JSON Serving)
/api/tree                              /api/tree.json                             200
/api/books                             /api/books.json                            200
/api/mat                               /api/mat.json                              200
/api/book/:code/chapter/:idx           /api/book/:code/chapter/:idx.json          200
/api/book/:code/toc                    /api/book/:code/toc.json                   200
/api/book/:code/mat                    /api/book/:code/mat.json                   200
/api/book/:code                        /api/book/:code.json                       200

# 2. Client-side Single Page Application (SPA) Route Fallbacks — valid app routes
# These must stay 200 rewrites (not redirects) so Next.js App Router can handle /book/* and /chapter/* client-side
/book/*       /index.html                   200
/chapter/*    /index.html                   200

# 3. Legacy URLs — handled by 404.html (Lost in Saṃsāra)
#    No catch-all /* here — Cloudflare automatically serves 404.html with 404 status for any unmatched path.
#    404.html (app/not-found.jsx) shows your "Lost in Saṃsāra" message + countdown + meta refresh → / (homepage).
#    This keeps homepage at 200 (no loop) and still shows the message for legacy URLs.
#    For instant server 302 to / (without showing message), use Cloudflare Pages Function instead of _redirects,
#    or uncomment the next line (will hide the message for legacy URLs and requires homepage exclusions):
# /*            /                             302
